    fix(int-ci-031): race-safe AC-1 clean-drift assertion (warm-up sidecar re-materialization)
    
    Root cause (proved from source): the AUG-096 boot warm-up enumerates
    namespace names once, then warms each through a worker pool
    (concurrency 4, per-ns timeout 30s). Each warmNamespace leg writes into
    the namespace directory: rebuildNamespaceIndex → .gitignore + .search/
    sidecar, EmbeddingCache.forNamespace → .embeddings/ (namespace-warmup.ts
    steps 3-4). The old waitForWarmupQuiet heuristic — two identical
    consecutive name censuses — observes NAMES only, so it can return while
    a sentinel leg is still in flight; the sentinel rmSync then lands, and
    the leg's mkdirSync/.gitignore write re-creates the sentinel path, which
    GET /api/namespaces truthfully reports as one onDiskOnly drift row —
    exactly CI run 38397048091's `{ onDiskOnly: 1, directoryMissing: 0 }`
    vs a clean local suite.
    
    Fix (test-only, no contract change; AC-3 untouched):
    - waitForWarmupQuiet now waits for the daemon's actual warm-up summary
      line (`[duckbrain] Namespace warm-up: ...`) on the child's stderr —
      we own the pipe — the deterministic completion signal (bounded 25s,
      falls through when warm-up is disabled).
    - new waitForCleanDrift: after the sentinel removal, poll
      GET /api/namespaces until `drift` is absent on TWO consecutive
      censuses, re-removing the sentinel each round to heal any late
      warm-up write; hard-fails with a named cause if never clean.
    - beforeAll timeout 60s → 90s (health ≤30s + warm-up ≤25s + drift ≤15s
      can stack on loaded CI hosts).
    
    The drift contract is not weakened: AC-1 still requires a fully clean
    census (drift omitted) before its POST/GET, and failure now names the
    race instead of surfacing as an opaque drift-row assertion error.
